The default address is on the loopback interface,
because the interface reads archives and runs their filters on this machine.
litar names the binary that serves the compositions;
file names an archive whose composition is imported before the first page.
@<litar-web@:command@:UI@/Command Line@/invocation syntax@=
{
    name: 'litar-web',
    options: [
        {
            name: 'addr',
            type: 'string',
            default: '127.0.0.1:8080',
            description: 'address to listen on',
        },
        {
            name: 'litar',
            type: 'string',
            default: 'litar',
            description: 'litar binary that serves the compositions',
        },
        {
            name: 'file',
            type: 'string',
            default: '',
            description: 'archive whose composition is imported at start',
        },
    ],
}
@
The options of litar, in the order of the usage in design/ui.md.
An action is chosen by giving its operand; agent takes none.
@<litar command@:command@:UI@/Command Line@/invocation syntax@=
{
    name: 'litar',
    options: [
        {
            name: 'agent',
            short: 'a',
            description: 'open an MCP server to handle the requests from agents',
        },
        {
            name: 'file',
            short: 'f',
            type: 'string',
            argument: 'archive',
            description: 'specify the archive file, find the composition and the node corresponding',
        },
        {
            name: 'literal',
            short: 'l',
            type: 'string',
            argument: 'chunk reference',
            description: 'print the blocks applied to CHUNK_REFERENCE literally',
        },
        {
            name: 'effective',
            short: 'e',
            type: 'string',
            argument: 'chunk reference',
            description: 'print the effective blocks of CHUNK_REFERENCE',
        },
        {
            name: 'depend',
            short: 'd',
            type: 'string',
            argument: 'chunk reference',
            description: 'list all blocks that depend on CHUNK_REFERENCE',
        },
        {
            name: 'reference',
            short: 'r',
            type: 'string',
            argument: 'item',
            description: 'list all blocks that refer to ITEM',
        },
        {
            name: 'print',
            short: 'p',
            type: 'string',
            argument: 'expression',
            description: 'evaluate EXPRESSION, and print it',
        },
    ],
}
@
